    "overview": "Against the sound 3...d5, Black grabs the f4-pawn but spends two tempi shuffling the queen (Qxd5, Qe6+) and leaves the king in the centre. This is not a sacrifice — it's a positional plan: develop with tempo, wreck Black's castling with Bb5+, clamp the centre with d4 and c4, and grind two permanent pluses — a big development lead and the weak, stranded f4-pawn — into a lasting bind. No risk, no material down: just a better position you can squeeze.",
